WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.890
Last time I covered Paw Patrol I convinced
you that this kid, Ryder, child genius inventor,

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.150
was recruiting homeless dogs to use as members
of his crew of rescue animals, the Paw Patrol.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.150
Why?

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.430
Well, because the missions are dangerous,
dogs are cheaper and more expendable than

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.880
humans, and stray dogs are the most expendable
of all.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.480
Now obviously, what Ryder’s doing there
is REAL bad.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.980
But the crimes of Ryder don’t just stop
there my friends.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.230
Not only is he putting his dogs into the direct
line of danger with little regard to their

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.480
well-being, he’s the one CREATING those
dangerous situations in the first place!

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.309
Get ready, all you good pups, because today
we’re exposing Ryder for the money-hungry

00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:45.379
criminal mastermind that he really is.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.579
Hello Internet.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:53.579
Welcome to Film Theory, where they’re all
DEAD pups and they’ll be replaced.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:57.179
Cus it’s just another day around Adventure
Bay.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:58.530
D-d-d-d-d Dead Patrol.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.980
So, it’s been a couple months since I last
covered Paw Patrol, and due to the blessings

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.250
of owning a four-year old discovering media
for the first time, I am still watching a

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.250
TON of the show.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.990
Now, if you’ve somehow missed this gargantuan
hit of a Nickelodeon series, the Paw Patrol

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:15.020
are a team of six puppies led by a boy named
Ryder.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.890
Each pup has a specialized set of skills,
vehicles, and tech that Ryder designs based

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.670
on typical emergency services.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.120
We have Chase the Police Dog, Marshall the
Firefighter, Skye the Aviation Pup, Rubble

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.670
the Construction Dog, Zuma for water rescue
and Rocky for Garbage collection.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.299
Episodes of the show are pretty classic action
adventure fare - there’s a problem that

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.810
needs solving somewhere in Adventure Bay;
the Paw Patrol suit up and say:

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:42.850
And then they use their technology, teamwork,
and winches…lots and lots of winches…to

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.040
make sure everyone winds up safe and happy.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.789
Have the farm pigs have run away?

00:01:46.789 --> 00:01:47.840
Call the Paw Patrol!

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.700
Is a plane about to crash land?

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.700
Call the Paw Patrol!

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.149
Has the villainous mayor of a nearby town
discovered an ancient relic in the jungle

00:01:54.149 --> 00:01:55.619
that turns them into a monkey?

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:58.539
Call the Paw Patrol!

00:01:58.539 --> 00:02:03.920
Yeah…as you might be able to tell, now that
I’m into the late seasons, the rescues get

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:04.950
REAL weird.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.780
DON’T EVEN get me started on the MER-Pups,
and the quest to save Pup-lantis.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:15.830
So that’s the premise of the show.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:16.940
Cute, simple, cut-and-dry.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.880
BUT, if you look even just a little bit past
the surface level, you realize that not everything

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.710
is peachy keen in Adventure Bay.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:27.220
In our last Theory, we concluded that there
have been pups in the Paw Patrol before the

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.750
main six in the series.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.320
Pups who died in the line of duty before being
callously replaced.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.940
Ryder himself was the mastermind of the whole
operation, finding stray and abandoned dogs

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.080
to recruit for dangerous rescue missions,
knowing full well that if they die, well,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.730
they can just be easily replaced.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.540
And on top of all of that, Ryder doesn’t
even pay the pups with anything but treats,

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.740
he keeps the considerable amount of money
generated from their merch sales, government

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.240
contracts, and literal stolen gold coins all
to himself.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:03:02.810
So, okay, the kid’s a bit unethical in the
way he treats his pups, not great, but overall,

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.940
Ryder and the Paw Patrol are doing far more
good than bad, right?

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.580
They’re solving problems, they’re saving
lives.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.930
It’s just what has to be done in the line
of duty.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:14.830
It might make Ryder a bit of a jerk, but it
doesn’t make him evil, right?

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:19.340
Weeeeell, Loyal Theorists, as I’ve continued
to watch more and more of the show, my suspicions

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.150
around Ryder have only increased.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:25.840
You see, in later seasons, a lot of the problems
plaguing Adventure Bay are caused by the various

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.120
villains of the show – Mayor Humdinger,
Sweetie, the Kitten Catastrophe Crew – but,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.150
the technology that they use sure looks a
LOT like the stuff that Ryder builds for the

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.150
Paw Patrol.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.140
And that’s because Ryder is doing much worse
than just taking advantage of disasters and

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.660
putting these innocent pups in danger to make
a quick buck.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.610
As the series goes on, it seems like Ryder
is the one CREATING the dangerous scenarios

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.410
that are putting everyone at risk.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.400
He’s selling many of the villains his technology,
he’s hoping that they’re going to create

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.710
more trouble for the Paw Patrol to solve.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:04:00.780
In short, Ryder is a war profiteer, he’s
an arms dealer who’s playing all the sides,

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.010
and in the process, he’s putting both his
dogs and his town at risk.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.431
All while he literally sits atop his Ivory
Tower, the Lookout.

00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:12.570
Now, obviously those are big claims, so let’s
step back and look at the proof that Ryder

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.650
is actually giving his tech to the villains,
shall we?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.810
In Season 1, we meet Mayor Humdinger, the
very competitive elected leader from the nearby

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.190
town of Foggy Bottom.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:28.210
We’re told that he always wins the competitions
he enters.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:34.280
Well, that is until the Paw Patrol rolls into
town and suddenly helps Mayor Goodway win

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:40.380
ALL the contests, from Hot Air Ballooning
and Cake Making to Cleaning up and Basketball.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:48.260
After that, Humdinger is no longer the Top
Dog, and no matter how hard he tries, he just

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.470
can’t seem to win.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:53.470
Goodway is always getting help from the Paw
Patrol, which means that he’s always playing

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.470
catchup.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.470
So far, so good.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.470
Just a little healthy competition, right?

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:01.030
Well, in Season 2, sick of always losing,
Humdinger pulls out a new strategy, A new

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:10.060
set of minions:

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:14.640
The Kitten Catastrophe Crew, who are now tasked
with getting Humdinger whatever he wants.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:19.390
They sabotage water towers, they make messes,
they steal giant gold chicken statues.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:22.930
I’m a Chicken *Bawkaaaa*
But here’s the weird thing about the Catastrophe

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:26.590
Crew, each kitten directly maps onto a Paw
Patrol member.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.840
Their pup-packs…ha, I guess, cat-packs?

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.080
have the EXACT same equipment as their Paw
Patrol counterparts.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.700
Cat Chase uses a zip-line and launcher, just
like real Chase.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.250
Skye has wings, just like the original Skye.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.650
Cat Rocky has a claw arm, just like the dog
Rocky.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.650
You get the idea.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.160
Now at this point, you might be wondering,
well…

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.090
Isn’t Humdinger just super tech-savvy?

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.681
Couldn’t he have just replicated Ryder’s
technology rather than it being given to him?

00:05:49.681 --> 00:05:51.350
And that’s what I thought at first too!

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:55.250
Except for one thing…Humdinger ain’t exactly
what you’d call a tech whiz.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.990
In Season 5 Episode 17: Pups Save The Movie
Monster, Humdinger tries to steal a Robot

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:06.150
Monster but just doesn’t understand its
control.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:13.530
And, in the Paw Patrol movie, his complete
ignorance of technology is what causes the

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.340
cloud catcher to malfunction and destroy Adventure
City.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:19.750
Now, those are just two instances, but across
the series there are plenty of examples where

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.400
he's just not that great with tech.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.310
That said, Mayor Humdinger DOES try to create
several inventions throughout his appearances

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:29.790
in the series, and they’re just AWFUL in
comparison to the stuff that we see Ryder

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:30.790
make.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.920
For example, in Season 3 Episode 3: Pups Save
The Soccer Game, Humdinger creates a remote

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.850
controlled ball in an attempt to cheat and
win a soccer game.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:41.790
And yet, his remote short circuits and breaks,
causing the ball to lose control.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.490
It gets so bad that the Paw Patrol has to
step in and save the day.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:48.780
Now, I don’t know about you, but a remote
controlled soccer ball seems just a little

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.260
bit less complicated than a voice-controlled
Cat-Pack with a freely-rotating, fully-operational

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.780
robot arm, and yet…

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.470
it malfunctions with barely any prompting.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.170
And this isn’t just a one time thing either.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:04.800
In Season 4 Episode 2: Pups Save the Cat Show,
Humdinger creates a robot cat to win yet another

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.330
competition, but when it trips and falls onto
the floor, it goes haywire, requiring the

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.660
Paw Patrol’s intervention.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.180
Later, in Season 4.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.970
This time Episode 16: Sea Patrol: Pups Save
a Shark, he creates a robotic shark that’s

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:19.320
powered by a wooden contraption that resembles
a Hamster Wheel.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:24.090
Not exactly top-of-the-line tech, but more
importantly, the stability of that shark is

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.180
ATROCIOUS.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.880
Its internal welding gives way and the shark
begins to flood after it gets hit.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.130
This is absolutely not on par with the quality
of engineering that we see with both the Paw

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:38.030
Patrol packs and Catastrophe Crew packs, which
get thrown around a LOT during the rescue

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.550
missions and dastardly plots.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:44.220
It only makes sense if Ryder was the one who
created all of the tech.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.400
Now, it would be one thing if the Kitten Catastrophe
Crew were the only bad guys to have identical

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.400
Pup-Pack tech…

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.729
At that point, maybe you can write it off
as a coincidence.

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:56.360
But the Catastrophe Crew are far from the
only rogues in the Paw Patrol gallery to use

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.889
tech eerily similar to Ryder’s inventions.

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:02.820
The Rescue Knight series introduces us to
Claw, an ex-knight and the villain terrorizing

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:03.820
the Kingdom of Barkingburg.

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:07.310
By the time the Paw Patrol faces off with
this guy, he already has his own personal

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:11.340
pup-pack with a claw that can grab things,
functionally and aesthetically identical to

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.250
the packs used by the Paw Patrol.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:18.060
Then in the Mission Paw series, we meet Sweetie,
the pet of the Princess of Barkingburg.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.750
Unlike what her name would suggest, Sweetie
is anything but!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.540
She’s the biggest cause of trouble in the
Mission Paw series, with crimes ranging from

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.860
theft to kidnapping!

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.410
Now, all of this is possible only because
of her vehicle and her Pup-Pack, complete

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:32.130
with a pincer, vacuum, and even a selfie stick.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.829
I guess you’ve gotta keep your followers
up to date on that #VillainLife!

00:08:34.829 --> 00:08:39.490
And, once again… all of it is strikingly
similar to the designs that Ryder has for

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:40.490
the Paw Patrol.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:44.319
In fact, when Sweetie suits up, her attire
matches the aesthetics of the Mission Paw

00:08:44.319 --> 00:08:46.759
outfits that the Paw Patrol is wearing!

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.519
Mostly black with colored accents.

00:08:48.519 --> 00:08:51.589
This actually has to be one of the biggest
pieces of evidence towards Sweetie’s gear

00:08:51.589 --> 00:08:53.699
being a Ryder original creation…

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:56.809
See, this isn’t a case of Sweetie seeing
the Paw Patrol’s look and liking it enough

00:08:56.809 --> 00:09:01.199
to copy it, or Ryder seeing Sweetie and digging
her outfit to make it into a Paw Patrol uniform.

00:09:01.199 --> 00:09:06.160
No, Sweetie puts this outfit on BEFORE any
of the Paw Patrol pups put theirs on, AND

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.139
the Paw Patrol suit-up before Ryder sees Sweetie
in the gear.

00:09:09.139 --> 00:09:10.709
This CANNOT be a coincidence.

00:09:10.709 --> 00:09:13.850
They HAVE to have been made by the same person!

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:17.730
But okay, maybe this sort of technology is
just super common in the Paw Patrol universe.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:21.680
Maybe Pup-Packs are something you can just
order from your local Best Buy… but again,

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:22.750
that’s not the case.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:26.990
As we called out in our last Theory, the Paw
Patrol are relative unknowns in this world,

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:31.779
they're only becoming more well known as the
series progresses BECAUSE of their daring

00:09:31.779 --> 00:09:32.779
rescues.

00:09:32.779 --> 00:09:36.899
Rescue dogs and technology for cats is not
something that exists normally in this universe.

00:09:36.899 --> 00:09:40.279
It is specifically being built by one guy:
Ryder.

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:42.410
“Alright, Matpat,” I hear you saying.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:45.839
“Sure, the tech used by the Sweetie, Claw
and the Kitten Catastrophe Crew ARE similar

00:09:45.839 --> 00:09:46.839
to the Paw Patrol’s.

00:09:46.839 --> 00:09:50.670
But maybe that’s just how technology looks
in this universe.”

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.879
That would be a fantastic explanation for
what we’re seeing here; a lot of times,

00:09:53.879 --> 00:09:57.860
the art direction of a show (especially an
animated show) can end up with character and

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.499
technology designs that look same-y.

00:09:59.499 --> 00:10:02.949
And while the Paw Patrol series definitely
has an art style that it sticks to, it also

00:10:02.949 --> 00:10:07.629
goes out of its way to show that different
technology made by different people look different

00:10:07.629 --> 00:10:09.730
compared to the Paw Patrol’s pup-packs.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:13.949
We already pointed out how different and almost
primitive Humdinger’s tech looks compared

00:10:13.949 --> 00:10:17.009
to Ryder’s, but there are other examples
throughout the series.

00:10:17.009 --> 00:10:21.290
For example, the Ruff-Ruff Pack are a group
of villainous biker dogs featured in the Moto

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.749
Pup series, and its three members all have
pup-packs as well.

00:10:24.749 --> 00:10:28.810
But their packs are WAY different from the
ones that we know that Ryder makes.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.420
Every pack that we’ve seen up until this
point looks very similar - they’re made

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:35.319
with clean, cylindrical or cuboid pieces and
their joints are easy to move.

00:10:35.319 --> 00:10:39.149
Plus, they’re all colored and feature iconography
that matches the pup or kitten that they were

00:10:39.149 --> 00:10:40.149
made for.

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:43.860
The Ruff-Ruff Pack’s gear, however, looks
like it was made with limited time and resources.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:48.209
These pacs are older, rusty, they’re made
using scrap metal, the joints are barely held

00:10:48.209 --> 00:10:49.949
together with screws and bolts.

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:56.589
This suggests that they were made by Gasket,
who we know is an amateur inventor.

00:10:56.589 --> 00:11:03.730
So, clearly the show’s art style cares enough
to indicate when technology is made by other

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:07.430
inventors…the Ruff-Ruff’s packs scrapyard
inventions, Humdinger’s early primitive

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.430
tech.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.430
But the Catastrophe Crew?

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.430
Sweetie?

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:11.430
There’s no other way to explain it.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:13.110
It HAD to have come from Ryder!

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.990
So, Ryder is clearly designing the tech that
villains like Humdinger and Sweetie wind up

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.559
using throughout the series, but why?

00:11:18.559 --> 00:11:22.519
Doesn’t necessarily seem like a great business
model to just be giving this tech away.

00:11:22.519 --> 00:11:25.630
But, just look at what happens once these
villains get a hold of it.

00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:28.779
In Season 1, the pup’s rescues can honestly
seem pretty trivial.

00:11:28.779 --> 00:11:32.059
They help the farmers out during the fall
festival, they gather up some lost bunnies.

00:11:32.059 --> 00:11:36.369
They help Mayor Goodway win a few competitions
and, in rare cases, they fight the occasional

00:11:36.369 --> 00:11:37.369
fire.

00:11:37.369 --> 00:11:40.709
It’s not exactly the high-stakes rescues
that Ryder was hoping for when he started

00:11:40.709 --> 00:11:42.940
the Paw Patrol to make cash off of disasters.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.259
But then, look at the escalation.

00:11:44.259 --> 00:11:48.199
By season seven, they’re being hired out
by royalty to protect the crown jewels as

00:11:48.199 --> 00:11:49.199
private bodyguards.

00:11:49.199 --> 00:11:53.339
They’re being asked by Mayor Goodway to
save stolen ferris wheels.

00:11:53.339 --> 00:12:04.389
Crimes that are only possible thanks to HIS
technology getting in the hands of the show’s

00:12:04.389 --> 00:12:07.619
villains.

00:12:07.619 --> 00:12:12.050
Ryder is clearly a smart kid, and a shrewd
businessman, and he takes his opportunities

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:13.050
where he sees them.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:16.290
Take Humdinger for instance - clearly the
competition between the towns was important

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.290
to him.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.800
And as time goes on, he gets more and more
discouraged as he loses because of the Paw

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:24.290
Patrol, to the point where he’s suddenly
willing to cheat in a way that he never did

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.290
before.

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:29.019
Think about it: In Season 1, we never see
Humdinger do anything shady or illegal - he’s

00:12:29.019 --> 00:12:31.420
just a REALLY competitive guy from a nearby
city.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:36.879
And yet, in Season 2, we immediately see Humdinger
playing dirty, as well as ignoring both laws

00:12:36.879 --> 00:12:40.370
and the safety of others as he destroys and
vandalizes property.

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:41.569
What’s changed?

00:12:41.569 --> 00:12:46.519
One thing… he now has his own minions in
the Kitten Catastrophe Crew, minions outfitted

00:12:46.519 --> 00:12:47.959
with Ryder’s tech.

00:12:47.959 --> 00:12:50.880
Ryder saw the competitiveness in Humdinger
and exploited it.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:54.709
He CREATED a villain in Humdinger and the
Catastrophe Crew to escalate the problems

00:12:54.709 --> 00:12:56.519
that the Paw Patrol could respond to.

00:12:56.519 --> 00:13:01.029
Suddenly, they’re not tracking down misidentified
cows in the snow - they’re stopping bonafide

00:13:01.029 --> 00:13:02.089
bad buys.

00:13:02.089 --> 00:13:05.709
Ryder can suddenly charge more for it, he
can get more publicity for it.

00:13:05.709 --> 00:13:09.749
He’s now building an empire for both his
exploited rescue pups and the technology that

00:13:09.749 --> 00:13:11.699
allows this stuff to happen.

00:13:11.699 --> 00:13:13.259
But it doesn’t stop there, friends.

00:13:13.259 --> 00:13:16.889
Ryder expands his little racket beyond Adventure
Bay and even Adventure City.

00:13:16.889 --> 00:13:20.889
He seeks out new locations like Barkingburg,
where he can give other misguided pups some

00:13:20.889 --> 00:13:21.889
of his tech.

00:13:21.889 --> 00:13:25.800
He creates new villains, and therefore, new
disasters on a scale that even he couldn’t

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:26.839
have dreamed of before.

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:30.850
Instead of a vehicle, Claw uses his Pup Pack
to find a magical dragon tooth that lets him

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:36.160
control a REAL ACTUAL dragon which he then
directs onto the people and city of Barkingburg.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.889
When the Paw Patrol avert that disaster, Ryder
couldn’t ask for better publicity - “Brave

00:13:40.889 --> 00:13:43.779
Pups led by Genius Boy Save City from Dragon”.

00:13:43.779 --> 00:13:46.779
With achievements like that under his belt,
just like that, Ryder has suddenly made himself

00:13:46.779 --> 00:13:50.199
a valuable new client for life in the Princess
of Barkingburg.

00:13:50.199 --> 00:13:54.760
But worst of all, the kid doesn’t even bother
to make sure the bad guys see proper justice!

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:59.489
He isn’t taking the steps required to prevent
these from happening in the future Sure, Sweetie

00:13:59.489 --> 00:14:02.679
is often put in the proverbial doghouse when
she’s caught, but she’s out again by the

00:14:02.679 --> 00:14:03.679
very next episode.

00:14:03.679 --> 00:14:05.549
And Humdinger and the Kitten Catastrophe Crew?

00:14:05.549 --> 00:14:08.459
Ryder doesn’t even bother to arrest them
when they’re caught red-handed!

00:14:08.459 --> 00:14:12.489
Instead, they’re just slapped with the catchphrase
“That Troublesome Mayor!”

00:14:12.489 --> 00:14:16.149
before getting off scot-free, ready to wreak
more havoc in the very next episode.

00:14:16.149 --> 00:14:21.839
Ryder is the city’s law-enforcement here,
arresting criminals would fall under HIS jurisdiction.

00:14:21.839 --> 00:14:25.589
But he DOESN'T, because that would be bad
for business.

00:14:25.589 --> 00:14:26.589
One thing is clear…

00:14:26.589 --> 00:14:27.920
Ryder is no hero.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:31.430
Not only does he put the lives of his pups
in constant danger with little regard for

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.649
whether or not they die in the disasters they
face, but he’s responsible for creating

00:14:35.649 --> 00:14:37.790
those disasters in the first place.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:42.290
In his greed, Ryder encourages these misguided
souls to cheat and commit crimes in order

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:46.889
to drive up business for himself, strengthening
his empire as it spreads from city to city.

00:14:46.889 --> 00:14:50.480
Ryder offers them advanced tech to escalate
their crimes to new heights, and then doesn’t

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.569
apprehend them to prevent future crimes.

00:14:52.569 --> 00:14:57.610
Ryder is the Paw Patrol’s worst enemy, the
true villain of this franchise, sitting pretty

00:14:57.610 --> 00:15:02.829
atop a Scrooge McDuckian pile of cash, while
he puts the lives of both his pups and innocent

00:15:02.829 --> 00:15:04.209
people on the line.

00:15:04.209 --> 00:15:06.889
Sure, they all may be good pups, but Ryder?

00:15:06.889 --> 00:15:08.679
He’s bad to the bone.

00:15:08.679 --> 00:15:11.259
But hey, that’s just a theory!

00:15:11.259 --> 00:15:13.850
A Film Theory!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:15.000
Aaaaand cut

